.\" Manpage for pcloud.conf(5)
.\" Operator-focused configuration reference for pcloudd(1) and pcloudc(1).
.\" Lint with: groff -ww -man -Tutf8 pcloud.conf.5 >/dev/null
.TH PCLOUD.CONF 5 "2026-04-16" "pcloud 0.x (pre-alpha)" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
pcloud.conf \- configuration file for
.BR pcloudd (1)
and
.BR pcloudc (1)
.
.SH STATUS
This product is
.B pre-alpha.
The Rust rewrite has not reached 1.0 and should not be run against data you
cannot afford to lose. The parity matrix in
.I C_FEATURE_PARITY_MATRIX.csv
is the canonical list of what is implemented, partial, or rejected.
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I pcloud.conf
(the operator-facing name for the on-disk profile) is the persistent,
user-editable configuration the daemon and CLI read at startup. It tells
them where to keep their data, how to reach the pCloud API, which optional
features are turned on, and how strict to be about security. A single file
is resolved per invocation; the merged result is validated before the
daemon accepts any work. You do not normally hand-edit every knob \(em
most deployments only change a handful of keys.
.
.SH CONCEPT PRIMER \(em FILE FORMAT, PRECEDENCE, AND DISCOVERY
Read this section before editing the file for the first time.
.
.SS File format: JSON envelope (today)
The Rust loader in
.I crates/pcloud-config/src/loader.rs
reads the file with
.B serde_json
and wraps it in a versioned envelope:
.PP
.EX
{
  "version": 2,
  "profile": {
    "environment": "Production",
    "paths":        { ... },
    "api":          { ... },
    "extensions":   { ... },
    "runtime":      { ... },
    "features":     { ... },
    "limits":       { ... },
    "mount":        { ... },
    "observability":{ ... },
    "resilience":   { ... },
    "data_residency":{ ... }
  }
}
.EE
.PP
Older documents are migrated in memory:
.IP \(bu 3
.B v0
\(em bare profile (no envelope) \(em lifted into a v2 envelope by
.BR migrate::migrate_to_current .
.IP \(bu 3
.B v1
\(em envelope without
.I observability
\(em upgraded with the
.B ObservabilityFlags::secure_defaults
block.
.IP \(bu 3
.B v2
\(em the current shape.
.PP
.B Honest caveat \(em TOML is not yet wired.
The man page and several references speak of
.IR config.toml ;
the
.BR pcloudc (1)
doctor command even looks for that filename. The actual on-disk parser in
.B pcloud-config
is JSON-only today. Two practical consequences:
.IP \(bu 3
Use a
.I .json
document that matches the shape shown above. The examples in this page are
written in JSON.
.IP \(bu 3
If you migrate to TOML in a future release, the envelope layout
(`version` + `profile.*`) will be preserved.
.PP
Tracked under the final-parity proof bead
.B bd-1du.10 .
.
.SS Precedence of values (lowest to highest)
The effective value of a field is resolved in this order; later entries
win:
.IP \(bu 3
.B Built-in defaults
produced by
.B ConfigProfile::secure_defaults
(sane, conservative, owner-only).
.IP \(bu 3
.B On-disk envelope
at the resolved config path, run through
.BR migrate::migrate_to_current .
.IP \(bu 3
.B Env vars:
.B PCLOUD_ROOT
(coarse path re-rooting) is applied first, then per-field
.B PCLOUD_*
overrides. See
.B ENVIRONMENT OVERRIDES
below for the complete table.
.IP \(bu 3
.B CLI flags
(e.g.
.B pcloudc --config
explicitly sets the file path).
.PP
Validation (`ConfigProfile::validate`) runs
.B after
every override is applied, so an unsafe combination
(e.g.
.B PCLOUD_ENV=production
with
.BR PCLOUD_API_MODE=plaintext )
is rejected with
.B InvalidApiEndpoint
rather than silently accepted.
.
.SS Finding your config
Run
.B pcloudc doctor
to see the resolved path, the active environment, applied env vars, and
directory-permission check. Example output:
.PP
.EX
config file        : /home/alice/.config/pcloud/pcloud-rs/config.toml  (missing, using defaults)
environment        : Production
api                : Tls bineapi.pcloud.com:443
paths.config_dir   : /home/alice/.config/pcloud/pcloud-rs      mode 0700 ok
paths.state_dir    : /home/alice/.local/share/pcloud/pcloud-rs mode 0700 ok
paths.runtime_dir  : /run/user/1000/pcloud/pcloud-rs           mode 0700 ok
paths.cache_dir    : /home/alice/.cache/pcloud/pcloud-rs       mode 0700 ok
durable auth       : disabled
audit export       : enabled
result             : OK
.EE
.
.SH LOCATION
Resolution order (first existing wins):
.TP
.B 1. --config <path>
Explicit override. Any path passed to
.B pcloudd --config
or
.B pcloudc --config
is used verbatim.
.TP
.B 2. $PCLOUD_ROOT/config/<file>
When
.B PCLOUD_ROOT
is set, every managed directory is re-rooted under it
(`<root>/config`, `<root>/state`, `<root>/runtime`, `<root>/cache`,
`<root>/plugins`). This is the recommended knob for per-tenant installs,
test isolation, and container filesystems.
.TP
.B 3. Platform default (from the `directories` crate)
.RS
.IP \(bu 3
.B Linux / *BSD (XDG):
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pcloud/pcloud-rs/ ,
falling back to
.IR ~/.config/pcloud/pcloud-rs/ .
.IP \(bu 3
.B macOS:
.IR ~/Library/Application\ Support/com.pcloud.pcloud-rs/ .
.IP \(bu 3
.B Windows:
.IR %APPDATA%\epcloud\epcloud-rs\econfig\e .
.RE
.PP
The parent directory must be mode
.B 0700
and owned by the invoking user. The daemon refuses to load a config file
whose
.I mode & 0o077
is non-zero (group/world bits set) in
.B Production;
it degrades this to a logged warning in
.B Development / Test.
Pass
.B --insecure-config
to override, which is acceptable only on a throwaway workstation.
.PP
Legacy layout
.RI ( ~/.pcloud/ )
is consulted read-only as a migration source on Linux, and only when
.B PCLOUD_MIGRATE_LEGACY_PATHS=1
is set. Migration never overwrites existing files in the destination.
.
.SH COMMON CONFIGURATIONS
Three worked examples. All three assume the JSON envelope described
above.
.
.SS Minimal home user
Take every secure default; only pin
.IR environment .
.PP
.EX
{
  "version": 2,
  "profile": {
    "environment": "Production"
  }
}
.EE
.PP
Every other field is filled in from
.B ConfigProfile::secure_defaults
plus the XDG path discovery.
.
.SS Headless small server
Durable auth tokens on so the daemon reconnects after reboot without an
interactive login, higher transfer concurrency, audit export enabled,
tighter retry budget against a well-known endpoint.
.PP
.EX
{
  "version": 2,
  "profile": {
    "environment": "Production",
    "features": {
      "p2p_enabled": false,
      "crypto_enabled": true,
      "durable_auth_tokens_enabled": true,
      "integrity_sweeper": { "enabled": false }
    },
    "limits": {
      "max_concurrent_uploads": 16,
      "max_concurrent_downloads": 16,
      "max_parser_frame_bytes": 16777216
    },
    "observability": {
      "structured_logs_enabled": true,
      "tracing_enabled": false,
      "metrics_enabled": true,
      "audit_export_enabled": true
    },
    "resilience": {
      "enabled": true,
      "rate_limit_capacity": 32,
      "rate_limit_refill_per_sec": 16.0,
      "breaker_failure_threshold": 5,
      "breaker_reset_timeout_ms": 30000,
      "retry_max_attempts": 3,
      "retry_base_delay_ms": 100,
      "retry_factor": 2.0,
      "retry_max_delay_ms": 5000,
      "retry_jitter_seed": 13498234234
    }
  }
}
.EE
.
.SS FAANG-ops multi-TB enterprise
EU-pinned residency, plugin-signed loader with one key, background
integrity sweep rate-limited to 60 files/min on a nightly cron, KMS
ready-but-not-wired
.RI ( see\ Honest\ caveat\ under\ [crypto.kms] ),
and a coarser (safer) retry policy that gives up sooner.
.PP
.EX
{
  "version": 2,
  "profile": {
    "environment": "Production",
    "api": {
      "mode": "Tls",
      "host": "eapi.pcloud.com",
      "port": 443,
      "server_name": "eapi.pcloud.com",
      "connect_timeout_ms": 3000,
      "read_timeout_ms": 10000
    },
    "extensions": {
      "plugins_enabled": true,
      "plugin_dir": "/opt/pcloud/plugins",
      "allow_network_capability": false,
      "allow_sync_control_capability": true,
      "allow_crypto_capability": false,
      "trusted_plugin_keys": [
        [26,43,48,5,175,10,64,23,88,201,3,2,1,0,0,42,
         17,204,88,231,12,44,200,99,100,31,16,15,12,1,2,3]
      ]
    },
    "features": {
      "p2p_enabled": false,
      "crypto_enabled": true,
      "durable_auth_tokens_enabled": true,
      "integrity_sweeper": {
        "enabled": true,
        "schedule_cron": "0 3 * * *",
        "rate_files_per_minute": 60,
        "pause_on_battery": true,
        "skip_list_path": "/etc/pcloud/integrity.skip"
      }
    },
    "limits": {
      "max_concurrent_uploads": 32,
      "max_concurrent_downloads": 32,
      "max_parser_frame_bytes": 8388608
    },
    "observability": {
      "structured_logs_enabled": true,
      "tracing_enabled": true,
      "metrics_enabled": true,
      "audit_export_enabled": true
    },
    "data_residency": {
      "allowed_regions": ["EU"],
      "strict": true
    }
  }
}
.EE
.
.SH SECTIONS
Every section below lives under the
.B profile
object of the envelope. Types and defaults are taken from
.IR crates/pcloud-config/src/ .
.
.SS environment (top-level enum)
Controls TLS enforcement and permission posture.
.PP
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb lb lb lb
l  l  l  l  l.
Key|Type|Default|Purpose|Env
environment|enum|\fBProduction\fR (via secure_defaults)|Development / Test / Production|PCLOUD_ENV
.TE
.PP
.B Why it exists:
gates several production-only validations in one flag. In
.B Production
the daemon refuses plaintext API, refuses group/world-readable config,
refuses zero-valued timeouts, and enforces owner-only managed directories.
.PP
.B Who should change it:
developers only. A laptop doing real work should stay on
.B Production.
.
.SS [profile.paths]
Where the daemon stores its files. All four keys are mandatory in the
envelope (but have serde-driven platform defaults via the loader).
.PP
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb lb lb lb
l  l  l  l  l.
Key|Type|Default|Purpose|Env
config_dir|abs path|XDG config|JSON envelope and auth-token vault.|PCLOUD_ROOT
state_dir|abs path|XDG data|SQLite store, audit log, sync DB.|PCLOUD_ROOT
runtime_dir|abs path|XDG runtime|IPC socket, PID file.|PCLOUD_ROOT
cache_dir|abs path|XDG cache|Thumbnails, FUSE staging, transient blobs.|PCLOUD_ROOT
.TE
.PP
.B Validation:
every path must be absolute; a relative entry returns
.BR PathMustBeAbsolute .
.PP
.B Who should change it:
operators deploying to non-default locations (e.g.
.IR /var/lib/pcloud ),
containers, or per-tenant multi-instance installs. Beginners should leave
it alone and set
.B PCLOUD_ROOT
in a service-unit file if they need relocation.
.PP
.B Interactions:
parent directories must be mode
.B 0700
or stricter per
.IR [profile.runtime] .
.B PCLOUD_ROOT
overrides all four at once.
.PP
.B Security:
.IR cache_dir
may briefly hold plaintext of encrypted blobs during FUSE staging; keep
it on owner-only storage.
.
.SS [profile.api]
API endpoint binding \(em where, how, and with what TLS posture the daemon
dials pCloud.
.PP
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb lb lb lb
l  l  l  l  l.
Key|Type|Default (Prod)|Purpose|Env
mode|enum|\fBTls\fR|Development / Plaintext / Tls|PCLOUD_API_MODE
host|string|bineapi.pcloud.com|TCP connect target.|PCLOUD_API_HOST
port|u16|443|Port 1\-65535.|PCLOUD_API_PORT
server_name|string|bineapi.pcloud.com|TLS SNI and cert-verify name.|PCLOUD_API_SERVER_NAME
connect_timeout_ms|u64|5000|TCP handshake budget (>0).|PCLOUD_API_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS
read_timeout_ms|u64|15000|Per-read budget (>0).|PCLOUD_API_READ_TIMEOUT_MS
.TE
.PP
.B Why it exists:
production transport policy is load-bearing; this section is where it is
pinned.
.B ApiEndpoint::validate
rejects
.B Plaintext
in Production, empty
.IR host / server_name ,
port
.BR 0 ,
and zero-valued timeouts.
.PP
.B Example (EU endpoint):
.PP
.EX
"api": {
  "mode": "Tls",
  "host": "eapi.pcloud.com",
  "port": 443,
  "server_name": "eapi.pcloud.com",
  "connect_timeout_ms": 5000,
  "read_timeout_ms": 15000
}
.EE
.PP
.B Who should change it:
anyone pointing at the EU data centre (`eapi.pcloud.com`); anyone
routing through a staging endpoint (override
.IR host
but keep
.I server_name
pinned to the production cert name to preserve TLS verification).
.PP
.B Security:
decoupling
.I host
from
.I server_name
lets you aim at a staging IP while still verifying the real certificate.
Setting
.I server_name
to an attacker-controlled value disables MITM protection.
.
.SS [profile.extensions]
Plugin loader policy. Disabled by default.
.PP
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb lb lb lb
l  l  l  l  l.
Key|Type|Default|Purpose|Env
plugins_enabled|bool|false|Master switch.|PCLOUD_PLUGINS_ENABLED
plugin_dir|abs path|<root>/plugins|Trusted plugin directory.|PCLOUD_ROOT
allow_network_capability|bool|false|Permit plugin outbound sockets.|PCLOUD_PLUGIN_ALLOW_NETWORK
allow_sync_control_capability|bool|false|Permit plugin sync control.|PCLOUD_PLUGIN_ALLOW_SYNC_CONTROL
allow_crypto_capability|bool|false|Permit plugin crypto access.|PCLOUD_PLUGIN_ALLOW_CRYPTO
trusted_plugin_keys|array<[32]bytes>|[]|Ed25519 pubkeys authorised to sign manifests.|\(em
.TE
.PP
.B Validation (ExtensionPolicy::validate):
relative
.I plugin_dir
is rejected. Any capability grant requires
.BR plugins_enabled=true .
A non-empty
.I trusted_plugin_keys
also requires
.BR plugins_enabled=true .
.PP
.B Who should change it:
FAANG-ops only, and only for a plugin that has been signed with a key
whose private half is under hardware control.
.PP
.B Security:
no signature verification is performed when
.I trusted_plugin_keys
is empty \(em the loader logs a warning and loads in "dev mode". Leave
empty only on a developer workstation.
.
.SS [profile.runtime]
Required Unix modes for each managed directory. Applied by the daemon with
.BR chmod .
.PP
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb lb lb lb
l  l  l  l  l.
Key|Type|Default|Purpose|Env
config_dir_mode|u32 (octal)|0o700|Mode for config_dir.|\(em
socket_dir_mode|u32 (octal)|0o700|Mode for runtime_dir.|\(em
state_dir_mode|u32 (octal)|0o700|Mode for state_dir.|\(em
cache_dir_mode|u32 (octal)|0o700|Mode for cache_dir.|\(em
.TE
.PP
.B Validation (RuntimePolicy::validate):
any
.IR mode & 0o077 != 0
returns
.B InsecureMode
\(em unconditionally, in every environment. Managed directories hold
auth tokens, sync metadata, audit logs, crypto staging, and the IPC
socket; there is no legitimate reason for them to be group- or
world-accessible.
.PP
.B Who should change it:
nobody, in practice. Tightening to
.B 0o600
on a file is fine; loosening a directory below
.B 0o700
is refused.
.
.SS [profile.features]
Product feature toggles.
.PP
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb lb lb lb
l  l  l  l  l.
Key|Type|Default|Purpose|Env
p2p_enabled|bool|false|LAN peer transfer. \fBReserved; no code path reads it today.\fR|\(em
crypto_enabled|bool|true|AES-256-GCM crypto folders, metadata encoding, share temppass.|\(em
durable_auth_tokens_enabled|bool|false|Persist auth tokens to owner-only vault.|PCLOUD_DURABLE_AUTH_TOKENS
integrity_sweeper|table|\fIoff\fR|See \fB[profile.features.integrity_sweeper]\fR.|\(em
.TE
.PP
.B Who should change it:
.IR durable_auth_tokens_enabled = true
is useful for headless reboot survivors. Leave off on shared or kiosk
machines \(em the token never leaves memory unless you opt in.
.PP
.B Security:
passwords are
.B never
persisted regardless of any flag. When
.I durable_auth_tokens_enabled = true
the token lands in
.I <config_dir>/auth_token
at
.B 0600
inside a
.B 0700
parent. Disabling
.I crypto_enabled
hides (does not delete) content in crypto folders.
.
.SS [profile.features.integrity_sweeper]
Opt-in, off-by-default background scrub that re-verifies recorded
size / mtime / content-hash for files under daemon management. Tracked
under
.BR bd-1du.4.6.1 .
.PP
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb lb lb lb
l  l  l  l  l.
Key|Type|Default|Purpose|Env
enabled|bool|false|Master switch. When false, no worker is spawned and no I/O is performed by this subsystem.|\(em
schedule_cron|string?|null|Cron expression for automatic runs. Parsed via the \fIcron\fR crate (6- or 7-field form); the daemon scheduler thread sleeps until the next boundary and invokes \fBrun_once\fR at each tick. Invalid expressions are rejected at shell construction and the scheduler refuses to start.|\(em
rate_files_per_minute|u32|100|Token-bucket rate cap. \fB0\fR permanently disables work even when enabled. Tokens accrue at rate/60 per second, capped at the per-minute budget.|\(em
pause_on_battery|bool|true|Pause scheduler ticks while any power-supply reports \fBDischarging\fR. Linux reads \fI/sys/class/power_supply/*/status\fR; macOS/Windows use the \fIbattery\fR crate. Unsupported platforms log a one-shot warning and behave as if this flag were disabled (servers and VMs keep running unchanged).|\(em
skip_list_path|abs path?|null|Newline-delimited glob skip-list. Invalid globs raise \fBio::ErrorKind::InvalidData\fR with a 1-based line number; there is no silent drop.|\(em
.TE
.PP
.B Who should change it:
operators running long-lived staged content on a server. On laptops keep
.IR pause_on_battery = true .
On developer machines leave
.IR enabled = false .
.PP
.B Interactions:
.IR enabled
gates the whole block;
.IR rate_files_per_minute = 0
is an override off-switch that takes precedence over
.IR enabled = true .
.PP
.B Scheduler:
when
.B schedule_cron
is set, a dedicated \fIpcloudd-integrity-scheduler\fR thread parses the
expression at daemon bootstrap and fires \fBrun_once\fR at each cron
boundary. The
.B pause_on_battery
check consults a platform power-source reader before every tick; when
the host is discharging the tick is skipped and a
\fIintegrity_sweeper.paused{reason="on_battery"}\fR event is emitted to
stderr. The manual
.B pcloudc integrity run-once
path remains available for operator-triggered scrubs. See
.I docs/parity/integrity-sweeper.md
for the full rollout plan.
.PP
.B Security:
per-installation HMAC-SHA256 paths are recorded in audit events \(em never
cleartext paths. Skipped-by-glob files are not audited. File contents are
never touched.
.
.SS [profile.limits]
Resource bounds. These are safety caps, not performance knobs.
.PP
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb lb lb lb
l  l  l  l  l.
Key|Type|Default|Purpose|Env
max_concurrent_uploads|usize|4|Cap on simultaneous upload tasks.|\(em
max_concurrent_downloads|usize|4|Cap on simultaneous download tasks.|\(em
max_parser_frame_bytes|usize|8388608 (8 MiB)|Hard cap on a single parsed wire frame.|\(em
.TE
.PP
.B Why it exists:
.IR max_parser_frame_bytes
is checked
.B before
allocation against the peer-announced frame length \(em a hostile server
cannot coerce multi-GiB allocations by advertising a huge frame.
.PP
.B Who should change it:
FAANG-ops on fast uplinks can raise the concurrent limits to 16\-32.
Embedded devices can drop the parser cap to 1 MiB. Beginners should leave
everything alone.
.
.SS [profile.mount]
FUSE / mounted-drive policy. Defaults enforce owner-only access.
.PP
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb lb lb lb
l  l  l  l  l.
Key|Type|Default|Purpose|Env
allow_other|bool|false|Pass FUSE \fBallow_other\fR.|\(em
owner_only_by_default|bool|true|Enforce owner-uid access.|\(em
.TE
.PP
.B Validation (ConfigProfile::validate):
.IR allow_other = true
and
.IR owner_only_by_default = true
together produces
.BR InvalidMountPolicy .
Enabling
.I allow_other
on a multi-user host also requires
.B user_allow_other
in
.IR /etc/fuse.conf .
.PP
.B Honest caveat:
the full mounted-drive runtime is tracked under
.BR bd-1du.4 ;
today this section is wired through to the FUSE adapter scaffold but
end-to-end mount parity is still in flight. Treat it as pre-alpha.
.PP
.B Who should change it:
never flip both to
.B true
simultaneously \(em it is a hard config error. FAANG-ops running a shared
jumphost: leave defaults.
.
.SS [profile.observability]
Telemetry toggles. Defaults: structured logs + audit on; tracing + metrics
off.
.PP
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb lb lb lb
l  l  l  l  l.
Key|Type|Default|Purpose|Env
structured_logs_enabled|bool|true|Emit JSON-lines to stderr (falls back to unstructured stderr when false \(em not silent).|\(em
tracing_enabled|bool|false|Span-based tracing. Behind Cargo feature \fBtracing-otlp\fR; inert in a build without the feature.|\(em
metrics_enabled|bool|false|Operator metrics endpoint on owner-only IPC.|\(em
audit_export_enabled|bool|true|Persist audit events under \fIstate_dir\fR.|\(em
.TE
.PP
.B Why it exists:
audit and structured logs are the forensic record; leaving
.IR audit_export_enabled = true
is how "who unlocked the crypto folder at 03:00" gets answered. Tracing
and metrics are opt-in because they cost CPU.
.PP
.B Honest caveat \(em OTLP endpoint is not in the config file today.
The tracing pipeline (
.IR pcloud-observability/src/tracing.rs )
accepts an
.I endpoint
and
.I sample_rate
programmatically but there is
.B no corresponding field in ObservabilityFlags.
If you need to point tracing at an OTLP collector today you must wire it
in code. A follow-up bead will add
.IR [profile.observability.tracing]
with
.IR otlp_endpoint ,
.IR sample_rate ,
and optional headers.
.PP
.B Security:
.B SecretString / SecretBytes
redaction is applied to structured logs unconditionally. The metrics
endpoint is gated by IPC peer checks \(em not broadened by this flag.
.
.SS [profile.resilience]
Opt-in circuit breaker, rate limiter, and retry policy used by
.B ResilientTransport.
Safe to apply to every endpoint; the default is
.BR enabled = true .
Absent blocks load via serde defaults.
.PP
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb lb lb lb
l  l  l  l  l.
Key|Type|Default|Purpose|Env
enabled|bool|true|Master switch.|\(em
rate_limit_capacity|u32|16|Per-endpoint burst size.|\(em
rate_limit_refill_per_sec|f64|8.0|Per-endpoint sustained rate.|\(em
breaker_failure_threshold|u32|5|Consecutive failures that trip the breaker.|\(em
breaker_reset_timeout_ms|u64|30000|How long the breaker stays Open before admitting a probe.|\(em
retry_max_attempts|u32|3|Total attempts incl. the first call (1 disables retry).|\(em
retry_base_delay_ms|u64|100|Initial retry backoff.|\(em
retry_factor|f64|2.0|Exponential factor (>= 1.0; < 1.0 rejected).|\(em
retry_max_delay_ms|u64|5000|Upper bound on a single retry delay.|\(em
retry_jitter_seed|u64|0x00C0FFEEF00D|Deterministic equal-jitter seed.|\(em
.TE
.PP
.B Who should change it:
FAANG-ops tuning SLO budgets. On satellite or flaky links,
.B raise
.I retry_max_attempts
and
.IR retry_max_delay_ms .
On batch workloads against a dedicated endpoint,
.B lower
.I rate_limit_capacity
and
.IR rate_limit_refill_per_sec .
.PP
.B Security:
disabling this wholesale is discouraged \(em it removes the client-side
cap that stops a buggy consumer from tripping server-side abuse
heuristics. Prefer tuning values over toggling
.IR enabled = false .
.
.SS [profile.data_residency] (optional, H11)
Region allow-list enforced at sync-root creation,
.BR upload_create ,
and
.BR set_api_server .
Defaults (empty list, non-strict) load cleanly on older envelopes.
.PP
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb lb lb lb
l  l  l  l  l.
Key|Type|Default|Purpose|Env
allowed_regions|array<string>|[]|Case-insensitive region tags (`"EU"`, `"US"`). Empty = permit any region.|\(em
strict|bool|false|true = hard refusal (`ResponseStatus::PolicyViolation`); false = warn-only audit event.|\(em
.TE
.PP
.B Example (EU-only, strict):
.PP
.EX
"data_residency": {
  "allowed_regions": ["EU"],
  "strict": true
}
.EE
.PP
.B Honest caveat:
enforcement helpers are landed in
.BR pcloud-backends::residency ,
but the daemon sync/transfer/account runtimes still need call-site
adoption in a handful of places. Until then, strict mode may miss a call
site. Tracked for the daemon integration pass.
.
.SS [crypto.kms] (enterprise; scaffolding only today)
Envelope-encryption wrapping-key provider selection. The provider trait,
the
.B AwsKms
and
.B HashicorpVault
impls, the PKCS#11 stub, and the in-process
.B unwrap_cached
TTL cache are implemented in
.IR crates/pcloud-kms/ .
.PP
.B Honest caveat \(em parsed-but-not-wired.
There is
.B no [crypto.kms] field on ConfigProfile yet.
Today a KMS provider is constructed programmatically by a binary that
embeds
.BR pcloud-kms .
The config-file surface for this section is documented here because it is
the agreed schema for the follow-up that routes the per-folder DEK
through
.BR KmsProvider::encrypt_dek / decrypt_dek .
Until that ships, the
.I [crypto.kms]
block is
.B not read
by the daemon \(em adding it silently has no effect.
Tracked under the KMS wiring follow-up in
.BR bd-1du.10 .
.PP
Planned schema:
.PP
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb lb lb
l  l  l  l.
Key|Type|Default|Purpose
provider|enum|null|One of null / aws / vault / pkcs11.
region|string|\(em|AWS region (e.g. `eu-central-1`). aws only.
key_id|string|\(em|AWS CMK ARN or key id. aws only.
vault_addr|string|\(em|Vault base URL (https only). vault only.
vault_path|string|\(em|Vault Transit key path. vault only.
pkcs11_slot|int|\(em|HSM slot number. pkcs11 only (stub today).
pkcs11_label|string|\(em|HSM key label. pkcs11 only (stub today).
cache_ttl_seconds|u64|3600|In-memory unwrap cache TTL.
.TE
.PP
.B Credentials rule \(em never in this file:
.IP \(bu 3
AWS credentials come from the AWS default provider chain
(IMDSv2, env vars, shared credentials, SSO). No AWS credential key
belongs in
.IR pcloud.conf ;
when the block is wired up it will refuse to load an AWS credential
field.
.IP \(bu 3
Vault tokens come from
.B VAULT_TOKEN
or
.BR VAULT_TOKEN_FILE ,
wrapped in
.B SecretString
internally, and sent as
.BR X-Vault-Token
over TLS. Never log, never persist to config.
.IP \(bu 3
PKCS#11 PINs (when the provider lands) come from the OS keyring or a
dedicated env var \(em never the config file.
.PP
.B Who should change it (when wired):
enterprise deployments needing central key custody, IAM-based
revocation, and KMS-side audit. Home users leave this section unset.
.PP
.B Cargo features:
.I aws
and
.I vault
are opt-in features on
.BR pcloud-kms .
A binary built without the matching feature rejects that
.I provider
value at load time.
.I pkcs11
is a documented stub and returns
.B NotImplemented
on every call.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT OVERRIDES
Applied
.B after
the file is loaded and
.B before
validation, so an override that produces an invalid profile is rejected
with the same diagnostics as a bad file. Unset / whitespace-only values
are treated as unset. Boolean values accept
.BR 1 / 0 ,
.BR true / false ,
.BR yes / no ,
.BR on / off
(case-insensitive).
.PP
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb
l  l.
Env var|Target key (notes)
PCLOUD_ROOT|paths.* + extensions.plugin_dir \(em re-roots every managed path under \fI<root>/{config,state,runtime,cache,plugins}\fR
PCLOUD_ENV|environment \(em also snaps api.mode to the new secure default unless PCLOUD_API_MODE is set
PCLOUD_API_MODE|api.mode (wins over the PCLOUD_ENV snap)
PCLOUD_API_HOST|api.host
PCLOUD_API_PORT|api.port (must parse u16)
PCLOUD_API_SERVER_NAME|api.server_name
PCLOUD_API_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS|api.connect_timeout_ms (must parse u64; 0 fails validation)
PCLOUD_API_READ_TIMEOUT_MS|api.read_timeout_ms (must parse u64; 0 fails validation)
PCLOUD_PLUGINS_ENABLED|extensions.plugins_enabled
PCLOUD_PLUGIN_ALLOW_NETWORK|extensions.allow_network_capability (needs plugins_enabled)
PCLOUD_PLUGIN_ALLOW_SYNC_CONTROL|extensions.allow_sync_control_capability (needs plugins_enabled)
PCLOUD_PLUGIN_ALLOW_CRYPTO|extensions.allow_crypto_capability (needs plugins_enabled)
PCLOUD_DURABLE_AUTH_TOKENS|features.durable_auth_tokens_enabled
PCLOUD_MIGRATE_LEGACY_PATHS|opt-in gate for \fI~/.pcloud/\fR \(em> XDG migration (set to 1)
.TE
.PP
.B Valid enum values:
.IP \(bu 3
.B PCLOUD_ENV:
.BR dev / development ,
.BR test ,
.BR prod / production .
.IP \(bu 3
.B PCLOUD_API_MODE:
.BR dev / development ,
.BR plain / plaintext / tcp ,
.BR tls / ssl .
.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Errors are printed on stderr with a JSON pointer, line, and column. A few
representative messages:
.PP
.EX
error: /profile/api/mode: value 'Plaintext' rejected in Production
  (production environment requires tls api mode)

error: /profile/api/port: must not be zero

error: /profile/runtime/state_dir_mode: too permissive: 755
  (managed dirs must be 0o700 or stricter)

error: refusing to load /home/alice/.config/pcloud/pcloud-rs/config
  (mode 0644 \(em pass --insecure-config to override in development)
.EE
.PP
.B pcloudc doctor
prints the resolved profile, applied env overrides, and a
ready-to-paste checklist:
.PP
.EX
$ pcloudc doctor
config file        : /home/alice/.config/pcloud/pcloud-rs/config  (v2, ok)
environment        : Production
api                : Tls bineapi.pcloud.com:443
paths.config_dir   : /home/alice/.config/pcloud/pcloud-rs      mode 0700 ok
paths.state_dir    : /home/alice/.local/share/pcloud/pcloud-rs mode 0700 ok
paths.runtime_dir  : /run/user/1000/pcloud/pcloud-rs           mode 0700 ok
paths.cache_dir    : /home/alice/.cache/pcloud/pcloud-rs       mode 0700 ok
env overrides      : PCLOUD_ENV=production
durable auth       : disabled
audit export       : enabled
result             : OK
.EE
.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.
.SS Config rejected in Production
The following keys cannot hold insecure values when
.IR environment = "Production":
.IP \(bu 3
.I api.mode
must be
.BR Tls .
.IP \(bu 3
.I api.host / server_name
must be non-empty;
.I api.port
must be non-zero;
.I api.*_timeout_ms
must be non-zero.
.IP \(bu 3
.I runtime.*_mode
must not grant group or world bits.
.IP \(bu 3
.I mount.allow_other = true
combined with
.I mount.owner_only_by_default = true
is refused.
.IP \(bu 3
Any plugin capability grant without
.I extensions.plugins_enabled = true
is refused.
.PP
Fix the file, or (for reproduction) set
.B PCLOUD_ENV=development
in a disposable sandbox.
.
.SS Permissions errors (0700 / 0600)
If you see
.PP
.EX
error: refusing to load: /home/alice/.config/pcloud/pcloud-rs
  has insecure permissions (mode 0755)
.EE
.PP
the daemon has found a world-traversable config dir. Tighten it:
.PP
.EX
chmod 0700 ~/.config/pcloud/pcloud-rs
chmod 0600 ~/.config/pcloud/pcloud-rs/config
.EE
.PP
The same rule applies to
.I state_dir
and the auth-token vault file under
.IR config_dir/auth_token .
The daemon never loosens permissions on your behalf; it only refuses to
proceed.
.
.SS Migration on upgrade
When upgrading from v0 or v1 envelopes the daemon migrates in memory and
leaves the on-disk file untouched. Rewrite the file by loading it once
with the current binary and letting a subsequent write (e.g. an auth
token store) persist the v2 envelope.
Legacy
.I ~/.pcloud/
contents are copied (never moved) to the XDG layout only when
.B PCLOUD_MIGRATE_LEGACY_PATHS=1
is set and the XDG destination is empty.
.
.SH SECURITY SUMMARY
.IP \(bu 3
Config file must be owner-only (0600 file, 0700 dir); refused in
Production otherwise.
.IP \(bu 3
Production rejects plaintext API, empty host/SNI, port 0, and zero
timeouts.
.IP \(bu 3
Managed directories must be 0o700 or stricter \(em enforced in every
environment, not only Production.
.IP \(bu 3
Plaintext password persistence is
.B not supported.
Tokens are persisted only when
.I durable_auth_tokens_enabled = true
and always in an owner-only vault.
.IP \(bu 3
Plugins without a matching signature from
.I trusted_plugin_keys
are rejected when the list is non-empty; an empty list triggers a loader
warning.
.IP \(bu 3
.B Credentials do not belong in this file.
AWS, Vault, and PKCS#11 credentials come from the OS / keyring / env
\(em never the config. When the KMS block lands, config-resident
credentials will be refused at load time.
.IP \(bu 3
Audit failures are fatal, not advisory.
.
